  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wildlife Without Borders-Western Hemisphere</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;This project aims to strengthen an existing network of citizens and youths committed to the conservation of the coastal wetlands of Matzatlan, state of Sinaloa, Mexico. Through this grant, the Grantee will: 1) consolidate the Environmental Educators Network by delivering training workshops on environmental education techniques, while promoting the implementation of on-the ground projects and the exchange of experiences and information between members; 2) strengthen the Youth Environmental Advocates Network by implementing a four-module training program on topics such as ecology, restoration, management and planning of wetlands, environmental awareness, outreach and education; 3) train residents and users of the Barron and Walamo wetlands on the sustainable use of natural resources techniques and economic and development alternatives; and 4) produce environmental and outreach materials for children and youth..&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
